<section id="about" class="py-16 md:py-20">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
    <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-10">
      <span class="font-mono text-xs text-terminal-accent tracking-wider">02</span>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-terminal-text">About</h2>
      <div class="flex-1 h-px bg-terminal-border"></div>
    </div>

    <div class="rounded-xl border border-terminal-border bg-terminal-surface/50 p-6 md:p-8">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-terminal-text mb-6">How I got into programming</h3>
      
      <div class="space-y-4 text-terminal-muted leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          I got into programming back in 2018 when I was in grade 12. I didn't have a computer, so I used to watch tutorials on my phone and try writing code using Android code editors. I grew up in a rural area where internet wasn't always available, so learning this way wasn't easy. At some point, I had to put it aside.
        </p>
        <p>
          When I joined Jimma University in 2019, I got back into it. I spent a lot of my free time in the computer lab, teaching myself to code and trying out new things.
        </p>
        <p>
          I graduated with a Computer Science degree in 2024, and in August that year, I joined 2F Capital as a full-stack developer.
        </p>
        <p>
          That's pretty much how I've learned programming from the beginning: try something, get stuck, figure it out, and keep going.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
